(83,236,'The Widal test is used to demonstrate rising titres of antibodies to flagellar (H), somatic (O) antigens in typhoid and paratyphoid fever.  An increasing O antibody level signifies acute infection, whilst a raised H antibody level may indicate the serotype of the infecting organism.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:36:34',NULL,NULL,'307FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
